WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.760
In this fictional story, the BHS bill is high. Charlaine investigates unnecessary lights under procedure. Preserve the refrigerator, handwashing water and required ventilation.

2
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:24.380
Only an approved, suitable reusable teaching visual, Charlaine says. No clinical single-use reuse. If policy is unknown, ask the supervisor first.

3
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:35.200
Confirm the approved master before printing. Prepare the teaching kit, but never delay urgent referral to save resources. Quality matters, not speed alone.

4
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:49.220
On dummy sheets: drawer A, printout A, approved master B. Old drawer copy or wrong file? Both are possible causes. Ask the person who printed and the supervisor.

5
00:00:49.520 --> 00:01:02.440
Request authorized leak repair, not handwashing restrictions. Explain the safeguard and rejection; give feedback and retry. Cards only; no actual repairs or clinical handling.

6
00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:18.260
Charlaine submits a proposal: verified version and suitable approved visual, with complete instructions and protections. An authorized facility decision is still needed. No savings or repair completion is claimed.
